  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Mob Rule!" id="f91b-99f6-34af-d0d6" hidden="false" publicationId="5e29cf46--pubd1e708" page="31">
      <description>If every model in a unit has this special rule, and the unit fails a Morale check or Pinning test (after any re-rolls they may have), roll immediately on the following table:


D6 Result
1: If the unit is locked in combat, it is treated as if it had passed the Morale check or Pinning test. If the unit is not locked in combat, it fails the Morale check or Pinning test.


2-3: If the unit includes one or more Ork characters (including Independent Characters), it suffers D6 Strength 4 AP- hits, and is then treated as if it had passed the Moral check or Pinning test. These hits are Randomly Allocate, but cannot be allocated to Ork characters (any excess hits are lost). If the unit does not include any Ork characters, it fails the Morale check or Pinning test.


4-6: If the unit has 10 or more models, it suffers D6 Strength 4 AP- hits, and is then treated as if it had passed the Moral check or Pinning test. The hits are Randomly Allocated. If the unit has fewer than 10 models, it fails the Moral check or Pinning test.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Waaagh!" id="4fe4-f365-e7e3-0d8b" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per game, the Ork player can declare a Waaagh! during his Shooting phase. This may not normally be declared on the first turn as a proper Waaagh! needs some momentum behind it. For the duration of that turn, all friendly Ork infantry units with this special rule has the fleet of foot special rule (not Gretchin).


If a unit rolls a 1 when making this Waaagh! movement. One model from that unit takes a single wound.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Waaagh! Energy" id="dc4a-98d1-edba-ea54" hidden="false">
      <description>Waaagh! Energy: The weirdboy grows stronger for every ork around him: (These are not cumulative, apply the best one available) 




While there are 10 or more ork models (excluding vehicles gretchin) within 10’’ add +1 to this model leadership characteristic. 


While there are 15 or more ork models (excluding vehicles and gretchin) within 10’’ add +2 to this model leadership characteristic and + 1 to this models BS characteristic. 


While there are 20 or more ork models (excluding vehicles gretchin) within 10’’ add +3 to this model leadership characteristic and + 2 to this models BS characteristic. 


However, every time this models rolls a double for a psychic test (whether the test failed or not), one friendly model (excluding vehicles) within 3’’ suffers perils of the warp.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Exhaust Cloud" id="ef65-90e8-5906-ce9b" hidden="false">
      <description>Warbikers have a 4+ cover save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ramshackle" id="8015-48ff-20db-6b86" hidden="false">
      <description>If a vehicle suffers a Vehicle Destroyed! or Vehicle Explodes! (wrecked) result, roll on the Ramshackle table and apply the result instead of the usual effect. If the vehicle suffers more than one Vehicle Destroyed! or Vehicle Explodes! result, roll one dice per result on the Ramshackle table, but apply only the lowest dice roll.


D6 Effect


1-2 Kaboom!
The vehicle is destroyed. All passengers and models within D6&apos;&apos; take a Strength 3 hit. Surviving passengers must disembark and take a Pinning test.


3-4 Kareen!
Move the vehicle 3D6&apos;&apos; as far as possible in a random direction (the Ork playere choosese if they roll a Hit on the Scatter dice). Then apply the Kaboom! result above. If the Trukk would careen into enemy models or terrain, stop it 1&apos;&apos; away.


5-6 Kerrunch! 
The Ork passengers take no damage but must immediately disembark. The Trukk is then wrecked.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tellyported" id="093a-d620-70d2-dbd5" hidden="false">
      <description>Any To Wound roll of a 6 made with this weapon has the Instant Death special rule. If this weapon rolls a 6 for armour penetration, it causes a penetrating hit, regardless of whether the armour penetration result was higher than the target’s armour value or not.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Dead Killy" id="a3d4-0982-88c1-f2d2" hidden="false">
      <description>Each additional Power Claw after the first two adds +1 to the Deff Dread&apos;s Attacks. (Deff dread still gains +1 for having 2 close combat weapons, so it can gain a maximum of 6 attacks and 7 with a charge)</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Burna Switch" id="675d-3239-d793-c3b2" hidden="false">
      <description>When a model attacks with a burna, it can use either of the profiles below. It cannot use both profiles in the same turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Scuttle Scuttle Blam!" id="873d-6da3-a6c4-165a" hidden="false">
      <description>Bomb squigs always hit the target on a To Hit roll of 2 or more.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Glory Hogs" id="6b7e-1c12-ddcc-da08" hidden="false">
      <description>Tankbustas must always attempt to shoot and/or assault an enemy vehicle if there is within range and line of sight.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Throttle" id="46b2-93fa-9e8c-6c86" hidden="false">
      <description>When the wielder is fighting in a challenge, his opponent reduces their Attacks characteristic by 1 (to a minimum of 1).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="High Voltage" id="cdd9-e4b7-10ea-85d8" hidden="false">
      <description>When the wielder makes its close combat Attacks, it can instead choose to make a single High Voltage Attack. If it does so, roll To Hit as normal, but resolve the Attack at double the wielder’s Strength (to a maximum of 10) for the purposes of that Attack.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rokkit Pack" id="c6a8-e296-10de-ce2b" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit made up exclusively of models with rokkit packs can choose to use them to Run 2D6&quot; in the Shooting phase instead of the normal D6&quot; even if it used them in the Movement phase. If it does so, every model in the unit must take a Dangerous Terrain test.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Trakked" id="b00e-deee-e2fb-7687" hidden="false">
      <description>The vehicle re-rolls failed Dangerous Terrain tests.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Chukka" id="e992-78af-5895-93b3" hidden="false">
      <description>Roll once each Shooting phase to determine both the Strength and AP of the bubblechukka, after the target unit has been chosen. For example, if you rolled a 3, the shot would be resolved at Strength 3 AP3.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Traktor" id="ffd6-b6ce-bb21-c471" hidden="false">
      <description>This weapon automatically causes an Immobilised result in addition to any other effects when it scores a glancing or penetrating hit against a Zooming Flyer.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ramshackle Monster" id="f245-e3bf-c3d8-4e32" hidden="false">
      <description>The Meka-dread and Mega-dread has a 5+ invulnerable save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Out of Ammo" id="eea6-6deb-f987-9bb2" hidden="false">
      <description>Out of Ammo: After it has been fired, roll a D6. On a 1-2 the weapon is out of ammunition and may not fire again during this game.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Jam!" id="d2a2-663f-b1fa-0807" hidden="false">
      <description>2D6 are rolled each time the rattler kannon is fired to determine the number of shots fired. If this roll results in a double 1, the weapon is treated as though it had been affected by a Weapon Destroyed result on the Vehicle Damage table. Note that a Mek may attempt to repair this damage as normal.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Zzap" id="e757-5b51-d139-5f9f" hidden="false">
      <description>Each time a Zzap gun is fired, roll 2D6 to determine its Strength, after the target unit has been chosen. If the roll is above 10, the shot is resolved at Strength 10 and the weapon Gets Hot on any To Hit roll of 1, 2 or 3. If a Zzap gun Gets Hot, the Wound is resolved against the crew. Zzap guns automatically cause a Crew Shaken result in addition to any other effects when they score a glancing or penetrating hit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sunder" id="543d-e04a-0677-3709" hidden="false">
      <description>This weapon may re-roll any failed Armour Penetration rolls it makes.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Aerial Assault" id="83f6-53ea-6198-cf83" hidden="false">
      <description>If this model moved at cruising speed it can fire all of its weapons.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Waaagh! Plane" id="fdba-2aa8-c92f-fe02" hidden="false">
      <description>During a turn in which a Waagh! is called, this model&apos;s Assault weapons fire twice as many shots as normal.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Strafing Run" id="8ea9-91f8-12d6-3221" hidden="false">
      <description>When shooting Assault, Heavy, Rapid Fire or Salvo weapons at Artillery, Beasts, Bikes, Cavalry, Infantry, Monstrous Creatures and vehicles without the Flyer or Skimmer type, this vehicle has +1 Ballistic Skill.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fighta Ace" id="8ccf-ca88-3f98-9b6f" hidden="false">
      <description>A vehicle with a Flyboss has Ballistic Skill 3 when shooting at Jetbikes, Skimmers, Flyers or Flying Monstrous Creatures.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grot Gunner" id="f716-08bb-7f7c-f3f1" hidden="false">
      <description>When a model with this special rule fires a big shoota or twin-linked big shoota, these shots are resolved at Ballistic Skill 3.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Skreamin’ Descent" id="c491-99ce-c8f6-d486" hidden="false">
      <description>Roll 2D6 and refer to the table below when making a Bombing Run attack with a Boom Bomb. The roll is made after the Blast marker is placed but before it scatters.


2 Faster! Waaagh! Uh oh...: No bomb is dropped. The flyer making the attack is wrecked, place the large blast marker centred on the position occupied by the target model – the marker then scatters 2D6&quot; (But not on a hit). Any units under the blast marker’s final position suffer a number of Strength 6 AP- hits equal to the number of models that unit has under the marker. The flyer is then removed from play and replaced with wreckage or a crater.


3 Clipped ’im!: No bomb is dropped. The flyer making the attack and its target each suffer a single Strength 9 AP2 hit. All hits on vehicles strike the vehicle’s side facing. 


4-9 Just like dis!: Execute the Bombing Run attack normally. 


10-12 Dakka-dakka-boom!: Execute the Bombing Run attack normally. In addition, the flyer making the attack may shoot any of its assault weapons at the target model’s unit. All hits on vehicles strike the vehicle’s rear facing. Any unit that suffers one or more unsaved Wounds from any of the attacks must take a Pinning test. Note that the flyer may shoot its assault weapons again in the Shooting phase and it can target a different unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mekaniaks" id="cbce-e6d4-d8cd-1217" hidden="false">
      <description>For each HQ choice in a Detachment (not including other Meks) you may include a single Mek chosen from this datasheet. These selections do not use up Force Organisation slots. Before the battle, immediately after determining Warlord Traits, any Mek that is not already part of another unit must, if possible, be assigned to any unit with the Infantry or Artillery type in their Detachment; a Mek cannot leave his unit and is treated as part of it for the entire battle for all rules purposes.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Turbo-Charga" id="769a-6b18-d180-f1c9" hidden="false">
      <description>The turbo-charga may be activated at the start of any Movement phase, after which the controlling player should roll a D6. On the roll of a 1 the Junka is immobilised (no saves of any kind may be taken against this damage). On any other result, the Junka gains the Fast type for the duration of the turn in which the turbo-charga was activated.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Piloted" id="98d7-b9de-2267-7b28" hidden="false">
      <description>Each Grot Bomm Launcha may only fire once per game, once its missile is launched it cannot fire another. The Grot Bomm works in exactly the same way as normal barrage weapons, except you may re-roll the Scatter dice and distance if you do not like the first result, but you must accept the second roll.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rumbler" id="f7bf-d5ce-120b-1358" hidden="false">
      <description>A vehicle may re-roll failed Difficult and Dangerous Terrain tests as long as it is moving at combat speed.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
