    <profile name="Twin-Linked Shoota" typeId="d5f97c0b-9fc9-478d-aa34-a7c414d3ea48" typeName="Weapon" hidden="false" id="34e1-e230-e793-88e7">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="6fa97fa8-ea74-4a27-a0fb-bc4e5f367464">18</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="a6383362-5aa8-4ff0-b1d0-00e059fc9d45">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="6abee736-f8d3-498e-97ac-a5c68445609f">6</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="077c342f-d7b9-45c6-b8af-88e97cafd3a2">Assault 2, Twin-Linked</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Mek&apos;s tools" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="4754-c9d5-41b8-ebf6">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">If a Mekboy or Big Mek is inside (or in base contact with) a vehicle at the beginning of his Shooting phase, he can attempt to repair a single Weapon Destroyede or Immobilised result instead of shooting. Roll a D6 - on the roll of a 4+ the result is negated. This could allow a previously destroyed weapon to fire in that shooting phase. On the roll of a 1, the Mek gets a bit carried away and the vehicle counts as shaken.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Kustom Force Field" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="7239-18e0-1c66-9c5c">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">The bearer, and all models within 6&quot;, receive a 5+ invulnerable save against any shooting attacks. If the bearer is embarked in a vehicle, then the vehicle receives a 5+ invulnerable save against any shooting attacks instead.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Grot Oiler" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="1657-b6c3-1464-964f">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">A Grot Oiler allows a Mek to re-roll a failed Mek&apos;s Tools repair roll. Remove the Oiler model once he has been used.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Gitfinda" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="4bf1-5c5f-be14-f899">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">A model with a gitfinda that remained stationary during its Movement phase has Ballistic Skill 3 until the end of its turn.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Weirdboy Staff" typeId="d5f97c0b-9fc9-478d-aa34-a7c414d3ea48" typeName="Weapon" hidden="false" id="bee5-826d-74b7-280e">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="6fa97fa8-ea74-4a27-a0fb-bc4e5f367464">-</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="a6383362-5aa8-4ff0-b1d0-00e059fc9d45">+2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="6abee736-f8d3-498e-97ac-a5c68445609f">Power Weapon</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="077c342f-d7b9-45c6-b8af-88e97cafd3a2">Melee, Force, Two-handed</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Ard Case" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="f95c-bef8-5d66-f3c5">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">A vehicle with an ’ard case no longer counts as Open-topped. Note that this affects its Access Points and Fire Points as detailed in the appropriate datasheet entry.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Boarding Plank" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="987b-05ea-7a34-4684">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">If a unit disembarks from an Open-topped vehicle with a boarding plank and declares a charge in the same turn, it adds +2 to its charge distance</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Deff Rolla" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="226b-460d-ad74-6029">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">A vehicle with a Deff Rolla may re-roll Dangerous Terrain test. 
Any Tank Shock (Not Ramming) made by the vehicle with a Deff Rolla causes D6 Strength 10 hits on the victim unit. If the unit elects to make a Death or Glory attack, it takes a further D6 Strength 10 hits in addition to the usual effect.
A vehicle with a deff rolla treats its front armour as two higher than normal when Ramming.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Grabbin Klaw" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="1886-f4f5-786c-a62d">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">At the beginning of the enemy Movement phase, nominate a single enemy vehicle that is within 2&quot; of the vehicle’s grabbin’ klaw. On the roll of a 4+, that vehicle may not move this turn. Flyers and Skimmers cannot be attacked by a grabbin’ klaw.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Grot Riggers" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="876b-36f1-aa59-f3b6">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">A vehicle with grot riggers has the It Will Not Die special rule.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Red Paint Job" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="fbd2-7bc4-9e72-2f6d">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">Ork vehicles with red paint jobs add +1 to their move in the Movement phase but do not incur penalties for the extra inch. For example, a vehicle could move 13&apos;&apos; and still count as moving 12&apos;&apos;.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Reinforced Ram" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="cd08-8f5d-6dbe-244e">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">A vehicle with a reinforced ram can Tank Shock and Ram, and treats its front Armour Value as two higher than normal when Ramming. Furthermore, the vehicle may re-roll failed Dangerous Terrain tests.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Stikkbomb Chukka" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="9564-3dd5-0299-b85c">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">The vehicle is armed with stikkbombs. Any unit disembarking from a vehicle with a stikkbomb chukka is treated as having stikkbombs for the remainder of that turn.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Wreckin&apos; Ball " typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="1b71-d803-7ba7-2baf">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">A vehicle with a wreckin&apos; ball causes a Strength 9 hit upon one unengaged enemy unit within 2&apos;&apos; of the wreckin&apos; ball at the beginning of the Assault phase on the roll of a 4+. The vehicle may not use its wreckin&apos; ball if it has moved more than 12&apos;&apos; that turn.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Waaagh! Banner" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="134d-0143-a16e-3ab6">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">All models in a unit that includes a Waaagh! Banner add +1 to the Weapon Skill characteristic on their profile.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Dok&apos;s tools" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="fe09-dd37-0232-8531">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">Confers the Feel No Pain ability to him and his unit.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Urty Syringe" typeId="d5f97c0b-9fc9-478d-aa34-a7c414d3ea48" typeName="Weapon" hidden="false" id="84f8-9ec1-4dbf-faa3">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="6fa97fa8-ea74-4a27-a0fb-bc4e5f367464">-</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="a6383362-5aa8-4ff0-b1d0-00e059fc9d45">User</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="6abee736-f8d3-498e-97ac-a5c68445609f">-</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="077c342f-d7b9-45c6-b8af-88e97cafd3a2">Melee, Poisoned (4+)</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Grot Orderly" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="387f-d08c-64f4-fb35">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">One use only. A grot orderly allows a Painboy’s unit to re-roll a single Feel No Pain roll.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Boss Nob Warbiker" typeId="2d6001b0-980e-46d2-bcc2-a9fc60109afd" typeName="Unit" hidden="false" id="40a9-5bae-1c45-e1f4">
